---
/**
 * SecureFormScript.astro — whole-form progressive-enhancement wrapper for
 * the owned secure-upload Cloudflare Worker (build plan §5.1: "Copy
 * (rename) | same | `SecureFormScript` → the shared Worker with
 * `siteId: 'golfraven'`"). Ported from `southern-wine-country`'s
 * `src/components/SecureFormScript.astro` @ 572ff7e, adapted:
 *   - to this site's design tokens (`src/styles/global.css`'s smaller
 *     token set — no `--gold`/`--wine`/`--space-*`/`--font-ui`, unlike
 *     SWC's richer stylesheet);
 *   - to detect "unprovisioned" via `src/config/forms-config.mjs`'s
 *     `isPlaceholderValue()`/`isValidWorkerUrl()` (a grep-able
 *     `TODO(owner)` marker, plus real URL shape validation) instead of
 *     SWC's `/^your-/i` convention;
 *   - **B1 (gate review, blocking): the form is INERT by default, even
 *     with JavaScript disabled or never binding.** All of its interactive
 *     content sits inside a `<fieldset disabled data-form-fieldset>` that
 *     the PAGE renders (see the USAGE snippet below) — a disabled
 *     fieldset excludes every descendant control from the browser's
 *     native form submission entirely (per the HTML spec: a disabled
 *     control is never part of a form's "constructed data set", on ANY
 *     submission, GET or POST). The module script below removes
 *     `disabled` ONLY once, ONLY when `formConfigured` is true (real,
 *     valid Worker/Turnstile config) — while unprovisioned, or with no JS
 *     at all, the fieldset stays disabled exactly as the server rendered
 *     it, and no native submission — carrying name/email/message to the
 *     page's own origin, which CSP's `form-action 'self'` would otherwise
 *     allow — can ever fire. The page's `<form>` tag also carries no
 *     `method="post"` (belt-and-suspenders: even a hypothetical bypass of
 *     the disabled fieldset would then default to a same-origin GET, not
 *     a POST — though since disabled controls are excluded from the
 *     submission regardless, no field VALUES would be attached either
 *     way).
 *
 * WHAT THIS DOES: one submit sends the WHOLE form to `workerUrl`, in-
 * website — no mailto, no third-party form service. FIELDS-ONLY (v1, no
 * file upload): POSTs directly to the Worker's `POST /submit` endpoint
 * with `{ siteId, turnstileToken, formFields }` — the exact request the
 * kit's `secure-upload.js submitForm()` builds on its no-files path.
 * Skipping that helper (all upload/compression machinery a fields-only
 * form never runs) is why `client/secure-upload.js` is NOT shipped here.
 *
 * SECURITY: every control that matters is enforced SERVER-SIDE by the
 * Worker and is NOT reimplemented here — Turnstile siteverify, per-site
 * CORS allow-list, rate-limit, and HTML-escaping of fields into the owner
 * email (`raven-site-kit/secure-upload/README.md`'s security checklist).
 * The client's whole job is: collect fields, attach the Turnstile token,
 * and POST once to `workerUrl`. NO SECRETS ship from here — the only
 * credential-shaped value is the PUBLIC Turnstile site key.
 *
 * DEMO/UNPROVISIONED-GUARD (this task's scope: "While the config is
 * unset, a form must not pretend to submit. It shows a clear 'forms
 * aren't live yet' state, and the build still passes"). While `workerUrl`
 * / `siteId` / `turnstileSiteKey` isn't a complete, VALID (S1: real
 * `https:` URL, no userinfo, no non-default port, a plain
 * `[a-z0-9.-]+` hostname) set of real values, this component (a) does NOT
 * render the Turnstile widget or inject its loader/challenge-iframe
 * hosts, (b) the fieldset stays disabled (B1, above), and (c) the submit
 * handler — reachable only if some other path re-enabled the fieldset —
 * shows a friendly "forms aren't live yet" message and makes NO network
 * call. The build stays green and the page stays usable before the owner
 * provisions the real Worker/Turnstile values.
 *
 * USAGE — the page's own `<form>` wraps its fields in a
 * `<fieldset disabled data-form-fieldset>` (see `src/pages/claim.astro`),
 * and carries every `data-*` attribute below as plain, static HTML
 * attributes — NOT stamped on by a script here. (This repo's own
 * whole-site invariant, `test/acceptance.test.ts`'s AT(7): no page may
 * ever carry an inline `<script>` with executable content, JSON-LD
 * aside — SWC's equivalent component used an `is:inline define:vars`
 * script to stamp its form's config onto the `<form>` at runtime, which
 * is exactly the shape AT(7) forbids here. Reading config from static
 * attributes the page already rendered avoids needing that script at
 * all — the module `<script>` below still reads `form.dataset.*` /
 * `fieldset.dataset.*` at runtime, only the WRITE side moved from a
 * script to plain markup.)
 *   <form
 *     data-secure-form novalidate
 *     data-worker-url={FORMS_CONFIG.workerUrl}
 *     data-site-id={FORMS_CONFIG.siteId}
 *     data-turnstile-site-key={FORMS_CONFIG.turnstileSiteKey}
 *     data-contact-email={FORMS_CONFIG.contactEmail}
 *     data-locale="en"
 *     data-success-message="..."
 *     data-unprovisioned-message="..."
 *     data-generic-error-message="..."
 *     data-verifying-message="Verifying…"
 *     data-sending-message="Sending…"
 *     data-turnstile-timeout-message="..."
 *   >
 *     <fieldset disabled data-form-fieldset>
 *       ...your text fields...
 *       <SecureFormScript
 *         workerUrl={FORMS_CONFIG.workerUrl}
 *         siteId={FORMS_CONFIG.siteId}
 *         turnstileSiteKey={FORMS_CONFIG.turnstileSiteKey}
 *         contactEmail={FORMS_CONFIG.contactEmail}
 *       />
 *       <button type="submit">Send</button>
 *     </fieldset>
 *   </form>
 *
 * `data-locale` (S3, gate review): which of `data-generic-error-message`
 * vs. the Worker's own (English, unlocalized) `data.message` the FR pages
 * show on a failed submission — see the catch block below. Every other
 * `data-*-message` attribute carries the page's own LOCALIZED text
 * directly (English on the EN pages, French on the FR pages) — this
 * component never hard-codes an English string that a French page would
 * otherwise show verbatim.
 *
 * `FORMS_CONFIG.contactEmail` is EMPTY in this repo today (deliberately —
 * see `forms-config.mjs`'s own `TODO(owner)` on that field: publishing a
 * personal address on a public site is the owner's call, not a default
 * this build makes for them). Every message is written to degrade
 * honestly with no address at all: no mailto link, no email text
 * anywhere, ever — each page computes its own `*_MESSAGE` consts from
 * `FORMS_CONFIG.contactEmail` itself (empty today → the no-email variant;
 * a real address later → the "email us" variant, automatically).
 */
import { isPlaceholderValue } from "../config/forms-config.mjs";

export interface Props {
  /** Deployed Worker URL, no trailing slash. From `FORMS_CONFIG.workerUrl`.
   *  Used here only to decide `unprovisioned` (build-time) — the page's own
   *  `<form data-worker-url={...}>` attribute is what the client reads. */
  workerUrl: string;
  /** This site's siteId. From `FORMS_CONFIG.siteId`. Same "decides
   *  `unprovisioned` only" note as `workerUrl` above. */
  siteId: string;
  /** PUBLIC Turnstile site key for this site's widget — decides
   *  `unprovisioned` AND is rendered onto the widget div's `data-sitekey`. */
  turnstileSiteKey: string;
  /** From `FORMS_CONFIG.contactEmail` — empty until the owner sets a
   *  PUBLIC contact address they're willing to publish (see
   *  `forms-config.mjs`'s own `TODO(owner)`). When empty, the `<noscript>`
   *  fallback below renders no mailto link and no email text at all —
   *  never a hard-coded default address. */
  contactEmail?: string;
}

const { workerUrl, siteId, turnstileSiteKey, contactEmail = "" } = Astro.props;

// Build-time mirror of the client-side placeholder check below. A site
// that hasn't been provisioned yet ships literal `TODO(owner)…` props —
// in that state, don't render the Turnstile widget div or inject its
// loader at all: a placeholder key is invalid on every domain and would
// throw an uncaught `TurnstileError` while shipping dead third-party JS.
// The unprovisioned-message path (submit handler below) fires on the fast
// placeholder check alone and needs no live widget.
const unprovisioned =
  isPlaceholderValue(workerUrl) || isPlaceholderValue(siteId) || isPlaceholderValue(turnstileSiteKey);
---

{/* Turnstile renders its challenge into this div once api.js loads — only
    rendered (and only loaded, see the loader below) once the site carries
    real config. */}
{!unprovisioned && <div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey={turnstileSiteKey}></div>}

<!-- Honeypot: visually hidden; a checked box means a bot filled every field. -->
<input type="checkbox" name="botcheck" class="hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />

<!--
  SC 4.1.3 Status Messages: this region is ALWAYS in the DOM and NEVER
  hidden/display:none — a live region must already exist in the
  accessibility tree when its text is injected or nothing is announced. It
  has no visible box until [data-kind] is set (see the scoped style
  below), so it costs nothing visually while empty.
-->
<p class="form-status" data-form-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

<noscript>
  {/* No mailto link, no email text at all while contactEmail is empty
      (the current, committed state — see this component's module doc). */}
  {contactEmail ? (
    <p class="secure-form__noscript">
      Sending this form needs JavaScript. Until then, email
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> with what you'd like to tell us.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p class="secure-form__noscript">Sending this form needs JavaScript. Please check back soon.</p>
  )}
</noscript>

{/*
  No Subresource Integrity hash on the Turnstile loader: intentional — the
  Cloudflare loader is versionless and self-updates, so a pinned hash
  would break on every rotation. Not injected at all when unprovisioned:
  there is no widget to hydrate, so loading it would only ship dead bytes
  and throw against the placeholder key.
*/}
{!unprovisioned && <script is:inline src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>}

<script>
  /**
   * Whole-form progressive-enhancement submit handler for every
   * `form[data-secure-form]` on the page. Astro bundles this once per page
   * regardless of how many <SecureFormScript> instances are present; each
   * form's config comes from the data-* attributes the PAGE's own <form>
   * tag was rendered with (see this component's module doc — never a
   * script here, and not from any value baked in below).
   *
   * FIELDS-ONLY (v1): posts directly to the Worker's `POST /submit` with
   * { siteId, turnstileToken, formFields } — the same request shape the
   * kit's secure-upload.js submitForm() sends on its no-files path, so
   * this build carries no dependency on that helper. Every server-side
   * control (Turnstile siteverify, per-site CORS, rate-limit, field
   * escaping) stays in the Worker; nothing here reimplements it.
   */
  import { isPlaceholderValue, isValidWorkerUrl } from "../config/forms-config.mjs";

  const forms = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLFormElement>("form[data-secure-form]");
  forms.forEach((form) => {
    const status = form.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-form-status]");
    const button = form.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('button[type="submit"]');
    // B1: the fieldset the PAGE rendered `disabled` by default — see this
    // component's module doc. Every interactive control (text fields,
    // selects, the submit button, the honeypot, the Turnstile widget) is
    // a descendant of it.
    const fieldset = form.querySelector<HTMLFieldSetElement>("[data-form-fieldset]");
    let busy = false;

    const workerUrl = (form.dataset.workerUrl || "").replace(/\/+$/, "");
    const siteId = form.dataset.siteId || "";
    const turnstileSiteKey = form.dataset.turnstileSiteKey || "";
    const locale = form.dataset.locale || "en";
    const successMessage = form.dataset.successMessage || "Thank you — your message has been sent.";
    const verifyingMessage = form.dataset.verifyingMessage || "Verifying…";
    const sendingMessage = form.dataset.sendingMessage || "Sending…";
    // Empty, not a hard-coded address, until the owner sets one (see
    // forms-config.mjs's TODO(owner) on contactEmail) — every message
    // below is written to read correctly either way.
    const contactEmail = form.dataset.contactEmail || "";

    if (!workerUrl || !siteId) {
      // Fail loud in the console for the site builder, not silently to the visitor.
      console.error("SecureFormScript: form is missing data-worker-url or data-site-id", form);
      return;
    }

    // Placeholder detection: an un-provisioned site ships a literal
    // `TODO(owner)…` (or empty) value rather than a real Worker/Turnstile
    // value. `isPlaceholderValue` is the SAME function
    // `forms-config.mjs`'s own `isFormsConfigured()` uses server-side, and
    // is imported here (not reimplemented) so the server's and the
    // client's "is this form live?" checks can never drift apart.
    //
    // S1 (gate review): `workerUrl` is ALSO re-validated here with
    // `isValidWorkerUrl` — the SAME shape check `forms-config.mjs`'s
    // `assertValidFormsConfig()` enforces at build time (https: only, no
    // userinfo, no non-default port, no path/query/hash, a plain
    // `[a-z0-9.-]+` hostname, no wildcard). A build-time-valid value read back from a DOM attribute
    // is re-checked here rather than trusted blind, before it is ever
    // used to build a `fetch()` target — the exact defense that stops a
    // scheme-less value like "raven-secure-upload.workers.dev" from
    // silently resolving as a RELATIVE path against this page's own
    // origin instead of failing loudly.
    const formConfigured =
      !isPlaceholderValue(workerUrl) &&
      isValidWorkerUrl(workerUrl) &&
      !isPlaceholderValue(siteId) &&
      !isPlaceholderValue(turnstileSiteKey);

    // The page's own `data-unprovisioned-message`/`data-generic-error-message`
    // (see this component's module doc) carry the LOCALIZED text — a French
    // page sets French copy here. The fallback (only reached if a page ever
    // omits the attribute) is computed from `contactEmail` itself, never a
    // hard-coded address: empty → no email mentioned at all.
    const unprovisionedMessage =
      form.dataset.unprovisionedMessage ||
      (contactEmail
        ? `This form isn't live yet. To reach us, email ${contactEmail} and we'll take care of it.`
        : "This form isn't live yet. Please check back soon.");
    const genericErrorMessage =
      form.dataset.genericErrorMessage ||
      (contactEmail
        ? `Something went wrong. Please email ${contactEmail} instead.`
        : "Something went wrong. Please try again later.");
    const turnstileTimeoutMessage =
      form.dataset.turnstileTimeoutMessage ||
      "This form's spam check didn't complete — its Turnstile key likely isn't configured for this domain yet. " +
        (contactEmail ? `Meanwhile, please email ${contactEmail} and we'll take care of it.` : "Please check back soon.");

    function say(msg: string, kind: "ok" | "err" | "info") {
      if (!status) return;
      // SC 4.1.3: set the styling attribute before the text, but never
      // touch hidden/display here — the region is always present in the
      // accessibility tree (see markup above), so this is purely content.
      status.dataset.kind = kind;
      status.textContent = msg;
    }

    function setBusy(on: boolean) {
      busy = on;
      if (!button) return;
      // Deliberately NOT button.disabled: disabling a focused button drops
      // focus to <body>, dumping a keyboard/SR user to the top of the
      // document mid-submit. Keep it focusable; guard with `busy` +
      // aria-disabled.
      button.setAttribute("aria-disabled", on ? "true" : "false");
    }

    function readTurnstileToken(): string {
      // The Turnstile widget script auto-populates this hidden input on solve.
      const input = form.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="cf-turnstile-response"]');
      return input ? input.value : "";
    }

    // How long to give Turnstile to produce a token before treating this
    // as an un-provisioned/misconfigured deployment. isPlaceholderValue()'s
    // TODO(owner) check only catches the literal placeholder string; a
    // real-shaped key that is simply misconfigured for this domain sails
    // past it and never solves — waiting for a token (not inspecting the
    // key's shape) is what detects that.
    const TURNSTILE_READY_TIMEOUT_MS = 8000;

    function waitForTurnstileToken(timeoutMs: number): Promise<string> {
      const existing = readTurnstileToken();
      if (existing) return Promise.resolve(existing);
      return new Promise((resolve) => {
        const start = Date.now();
        const poll = window.setInterval(() => {
          const token = readTurnstileToken();
          if (token || Date.now() - start >= timeoutMs) {
            window.clearInterval(poll);
            resolve(token);
          }
        }, 200);
      });
    }

    function collectFields(): Record<string, string> {
      const fields: Record<string, string> = {};
      // Skip the honeypot and the Turnstile token — the token rides in
      // the top-level request body, not inside formFields.
      const skip = new Set(["botcheck", "cf-turnstile-response"]);
      new FormData(form).forEach((value, key) => {
        if (skip.has(key) || value instanceof File) return;
        fields[key] = String(value);
      });
      return fields;
    }

    form.addEventListener("submit", async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (busy) return;

      // Analytics values are captured HERE, at the top, because
      // form.reset() runs immediately after the success message and
      // would blank them. This is a positive, literal pick of exactly the
      // closed-set fields — never the whole FormData, which also holds
      // the sender's name, email and free-text message.
      const _fd = new FormData(form);
      const _analytics = {
        request_type: String(_fd.get("request_type") || ""),
        relationship: String(_fd.get("relationship") || ""),
        topic: String(_fd.get("topic") || ""),
      };

      // Honeypot: if the hidden checkbox was checked, silently pretend success.
      const bot = form.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="botcheck"]');
      if (bot && bot.checked) {
        say(successMessage, "ok");
        form.reset();
        return;
      }

      // Native validity first.
      if (!form.checkValidity()) {
        form.reportValidity();
        return;
      }

      // Fast path: forms aren't live yet (unprovisioned OR an invalid
      // workerUrl — S1) → friendly message, NO network call. This is
      // reachable only if the fieldset was somehow re-enabled without
      // `formConfigured` being true (it never is, from this script), so
      // it's a second, independent layer under B1's fieldset-disabled
      // defense, not the only one.
      if (!formConfigured) {
        say(unprovisionedMessage, "info");
        return;
      }

      setBusy(true);
      say(verifyingMessage, "info");

      // Slow path: a real-shaped key misconfigured for this domain sails
      // past the check above, then never solves — wait for an actual
      // token (or the ready timeout) instead of trusting the key's shape.
      const turnstileToken = await waitForTurnstileToken(TURNSTILE_READY_TIMEOUT_MS);
      if (!turnstileToken) {
        setBusy(false);
        say(turnstileTimeoutMessage, "info");
        return;
      }

      say(sendingMessage, "info");

      try {
        // FIELDS-ONLY: post straight to the Worker's /submit — the only
        // host the client ever talks to. No secrets in this body; the
        // Worker does the siteverify, CORS, and rate-limit.
        const res = await fetch(`${workerUrl}/submit`, {
          method: "POST",
          headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
          body: JSON.stringify({
            siteId,
            turnstileToken,
            formFields: collectFields(),
          }),
        });
        const data = await res.json().catch(() => ({}) as { success?: boolean; message?: string });
        // Honesty over politeness: success ONLY when the Worker reports it.
        if (!res.ok || !data.success) {
          throw new Error(data.message || "Could not send your submission. Please try again shortly.");
        }
        say(successMessage, "ok");

        // Conversion — anchored HERE and nowhere else.
        //
        // say(successMessage, 'ok') appears TWICE in this file with
        // identical arguments: once in the honeypot branch above, which
        // deliberately feigns success for bots, and once here. Anchoring
        // analytics on that call, on the status element, or on any DOM
        // mutation would count every bot as a conversion. This point is
        // reachable ONLY after the Worker returned success:2xx with
        // data.success true — the honeypot returns far above, the
        // unprovisioned path returns above, and a failed Turnstile
        // returns above.
        //
        // Emitted BEFORE form.reset(), reading the values hoisted at the
        // top of this handler, because reset() blanks them.
        try {
          const win = window as unknown as {
            ccAnalytics?: { track: (name: string, params?: Record<string, unknown>) => void };
          };
          if (win.ccAnalytics) {
            if (_analytics.request_type === "feedback") {
              win.ccAnalytics.track("feedback_submit", { topic: _analytics.topic });
            } else {
              win.ccAnalytics.track("generate_lead", {
                request_type: _analytics.request_type,
                relationship: _analytics.relationship,
              });
            }
          }
        } catch (_e) {
          /* analytics must never affect delivery */
        }

        form.reset();
      } catch (err) {
        // S3 (gate review): the Worker's `data.message` (thrown above) is
        // plain, unlocalized English — this shared backend has no notion
        // of the visitor's page language. On an FR page, showing it
        // verbatim would mix English into an otherwise-French status
        // message; `genericErrorMessage` (locale-appropriate, computed by
        // the page) is shown instead. EN pages keep the Worker's own,
        // more specific message.
        const rawMessage = err instanceof Error ? err.message : "";
        const message = locale === "fr" ? "" : rawMessage;
        say(message || genericErrorMessage, "err");
      } finally {
        setBusy(false);
      }
    });

    // B1: enable the fieldset EXACTLY ONCE, on load, and ONLY when the
    // form is genuinely configured. While unprovisioned (or misconfigured
    // — an invalid workerUrl counts as unprovisioned here), it stays
    // disabled exactly as the server rendered it, forever, for this page
    // view — no native submission of any kind can ever carry field
    // values off this page.
    //
    // S-b (re-gate): this runs AFTER `form.addEventListener("submit", ...)`
    // above, deliberately — not before. Both statements are synchronous
    // and run in the same task before the browser can ever dispatch a
    // "submit" event (there is no `await` between them), so this ordering
    // makes no behavioural difference to whether the listener is attached
    // in time. It matters for a different reason: reading top-to-bottom,
    // the listener that will actually handle a real submission is now
    // established before the one statement that makes the form
    // submittable at all — so a reviewer (or a future edit) never has a
    // window where the fieldset could read as "enabled, but nothing is
    // listening yet" from the source order alone.
    if (fieldset && formConfigured) {
      fieldset.disabled = false;
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  /* Honeypot — off-screen, unreachable by keyboard, hidden from AT. */
  .hp {
    position: absolute;
    left: -9999px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  /* Status region: no visual footprint until a message exists. Do NOT
     reach for `.form-status:empty { display:none }` — that removes the
     region from the accessibility tree at the exact moment content is
     injected and re-breaks SC 4.1.3 the same way a `hidden` attribute
     would. */
  .form-status {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    border-radius: 0.3rem;
  }
  .form-status[data-kind] {
    padding: 0.65em 0.85em;
  }
  .form-status[data-kind="ok"] {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #2e6b3f 14%, var(--paper));
    color: #1e4620;
    border-left: 3px solid #2e6b3f;
  }
  .form-status[data-kind="err"] {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #b23a3a 12%, var(--paper));
    color: #7a2323;
    border-left: 3px solid #b23a3a;
  }
  .form-status[data-kind="info"] {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, var(--paper));
    color: var(--ink);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .secure-form__noscript {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .secure-form__noscript a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Turnstile widget spacing — sits above the submit button. */
  .cf-turnstile {
    margin-block: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
